  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda - Rollout of a&#x2018;last mile health network&#x2019;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Healthy Entrepreneurs group (HE) is a social enterprise. HE has established a franchise network of micro Community Health Entrepreneurs (CHE) to provide people in rural areas of Africa with basic healthcare products and services. These would otherwise be difficult to access. HE wants to expand in Uganda and Kenya to achieve economies of scale and build a commercial business case. In Uganda and Kenya, a &#x2018;last-mile&#x2019; distribution network of around 4,000 CHEs, serving around 1 million families with affordable products and services, has already been established. Because health services are offered closer to home, families save a lot of money on transport costs. The combination of an efficient supply chain, the use of customer-friendly technology and the cooperation with local health entrepreneurs lead to significant improvement in the rural healthcare service. HE&#x2019;s goal is to expand to 16,400 CHEs in Uganda and Kenya in 2025 and to serve 3,8 million families. DGGF&#x2019;s loan will support Healthy Entrepreneurs B.V. with their goals. The loan finances, among other things, health product supplies, prefinancing of CHEs product baskets, office costs, transport costs, selection and training costs, and tablets.</narrative>
  </description>
